6 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182580" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411156 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411156 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨Y)⇔X\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-4}} |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411156 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7dce07e5-2c84-5040-bb81-50a03090839e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411156 #edb/ref 1074 "According to the definition of the biconditional, \n\n- $P⇔Q$ is true if $P⇒Q$ **and** $Q⇒P.$ Otherwise, it is false.\n\n- In other words, $P⇔Q$ is true if $P$ and $Q$ have the same truth values. Otherwise, it is false.\n\nFirst, we add a columns for $X∨Y$ and $¬(X∨Y):$\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,X∨Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨Y)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nFinally, we add a column for $¬(X∨Y)⇔X.$ \n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\,X∨Y\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨Y)\\,$ | $\\,¬(X∨Y)⇔X\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411157 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186411147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411157 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182523" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411157 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411157 #edb/ref 1071 "$¬(Y⇔X)≡$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411157 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "96aebafe-ff76-58ac-a04c-e47b82d4e2a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186411157 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we use the definition of the biconditional statement to write the equivalence as a conjunction of implications: \n\n$$\n¬(Y⇔X)≡¬[(Y⇒X)∧(X⇒Y)]\n$$\n\nNow, we represent all the implications using disjunctions and negations:\n\n$$\n¬[(Y⇒X)∧(X⇒Y)]≡¬[(¬Y∨X)∧(¬X∨Y)]\n$$\n\nNext, we use De Morgan's laws:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬[(¬Y∨X)∧(¬X∨Y)] & ≡¬(¬Y∨X)∨¬(¬X∨Y) \\\\  & ≡(¬¬Y∧¬X)∨(¬¬X∧¬Y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify the double negations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(¬¬Y∧¬X)∨(¬¬X∧¬Y) & ≡(Y∧¬X)∨(X∧¬Y)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412665 #edb/ref 1080 "\\text{F}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412665 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412665 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "06c6a545-c229-5f5d-870c-b79d9c9a59c9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412666 #edb/ref 1080 "\\text{F}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412666 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186412666 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4ca4de5e-af8a-5c24-a605-1616e6c252f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
